# Source exposure and coverage

The exact root padding proposal and its freeze were read fully before this review. The frozen chain derivation was authored and read in the preceding task; its exact identity was preserved, and its geometry/access, positive blocks, Gram and composition sections were reread here. It remains a separately pending dependency. Qualified static-bias and bus source scopes were reused from their preceding complete reads and exact hashes refreshed. This is an exposed same-model/context mathematical check, not blind or different-model-family verification.

The fresh chain-file read ranges were 1-85 and 127-225. Lines 86-126 were reused unchanged from the immediately preceding complete proof read. The launch manifest's compressed section labels are not a claim that every line of sections 1-4 was freshly reread during this padding task; the exact ranges here control that coverage statement. The full necessary argument was already covered at the same frozen identity, and the present review does not certify the spectral induction anew.

Seven exact source/provenance files are copied under `source_snapshots/` and listed with original paths, bytes and SHA-256 values in `SOURCE_MANIFEST.json`. No current Git HEAD claim is made; no Git operation was used. The chain derivation and its original freeze remain unchanged. This task does not freshly verify every historical parent executable or every member of those older freezes.

After the initial review draft and checker source were written, root suggested a separate known-decoupled-filler-drift extension. It is explicitly attributed and proved in REVIEW section 4, with its different full comparator. It did not replace the frozen idle-filler proposal. The program was not modified or rerun to manufacture evidence for that extension.

The new checker and launcher were written independently of historical executables. One actual execution completed with source-at-launch, complete actual argv/cwd/timing/result and streams. The finite source and complete results were read after execution. All final hashes are verified before sealing. Read coverage and execution support provenance; they do not substitute for the path and operator proofs.

The existing workhorse/physics-claim-reviewer scope was reused. No model or effort override, subagent, retained audit, publication, graph/cache/lock operation, canonical/source edit outside this output, physical axiom change, editable prompt edit or other-chat mutation occurred. The outward-direction and corner-port qualifications are explicit findings, not silently inferred physical permissions.
